{
  "_comment": "Default home layouts, in half-cell tracks (TRACKS_PER_CELL = 2), authored per tier against the square-cell track counts. Placement keys are a tier (micro, tiny, small, medium, large, xlarge, xxlarge; include/ui_breakpoint.h) or a tier on one measured grid ('<tier>@<cols>x<rows>'), which wins over the bare tier on that grid. 'anchors' is the landscape table; 'variants' holds per-layout tables keyed by LayoutManager::variant_chain(). Any key may also name a capability subject ('<tier>+<subject>', '<tier>@<cols>x<rows>+<subject>'): while that subject is non-zero it wins over the same key without it, in placements, slot regions, 'disabled' and 'gaps' alike. A tool changer ('+ams_is_tool_changer') places no temperature tiles, since the tool switcher shows each tool's temperature and the printer image's chips show the bed; the space they leave is a declared gap, beside the printer image wherever the tier's arrangement allows. A fixed anchor sits where its key says. A 'slot' fills its region with the first alternative that fits and whose lead cell has a qualifying candidate (gate open, every 'requires' subject non-zero, not already placed); the last alternative is taken whenever it fits. Each cell takes the first qualifying candidate of its list, so cells sharing a list fill in the order they are written and any cell left over stays empty; slots resolve in table order. 'at' is [col, row, colspan, rowspan] relative to the region. Candidate lists hold only hardware- or capability-gated widgets, so a printer without the hardware gets an empty cell, never a stand-in. Widgets not placed are auto-placed at their registry default_enabled, so 'disabled' switches a default-enabled widget off where a tier has no room for it. 'gaps' lists, per placement key, the [col, row, colspan, rowspan] blocks left empty on purpose: every track is a tile, a declared gap, or a slot cell with no qualifying candidate (tests/unit/test_default_layout.cpp coverage case). The resolver does not read 'gaps'.",
